                <pb facs="0798" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-09T18:00:00+08:00">June 9, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received, June 9—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. Legation’s 245, June 6, 5 p.m. Following telegram has been received from
                    Vice Consul Yunnanfu: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 8, 10 a.m. Referring to my telegram of June 5, 3 p.m., American
                            citizens residing Tatsienlu are safe at Chungking.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
